# BuildKit does NOT match nested directories with a bare `node_modules`/`dist`
# pattern — it would leak host node_modules / stale build output into the build
# context. Use `**/` so every workspace's copy is excluded (Bun-1.3 gotcha).
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.expo
**/coverage
# Every workspace's env files, not just the root's: `COPY packages/backend`
# would otherwise put a local packages/backend/.env into a build layer. The
# build reads no .env file, examples included.
**/.env
**/.env.*
*.log
.git
# Local worktrees: other checkouts, with their own env files and node_modules.
.worktrees
.github
.vscode
.idea
.claude
docs
**/*.test.ts
**/__tests__
sst.config.ts
.do
